# Scope-level: the snapshot's last two bytes are \xff\xfe, which no UTF-8
# decoder accepts. This tree is pass-1 byte for byte apart from them.
#
# Python's open().read() decoded strictly and died on those bytes (exit 1); Go's
# string(data) keeps them, and the FK and index regexes go on matching the valid
# remainder — so the run reports on the part of the snapshot it could read and
# says nothing about the part it could not (#262 finding 3).
#
# It is built on pass-1 rather than fire-1 on purpose. On fire-1 the FK finding
# survives the bad bytes and the checker exits 1 both before and after the fix,
# which is no RED at all; on pass-1 the difference is exactly exit 0 -> exit 1.
#
# Pinned to the detector's header sentence, so the pin holds whatever the
# decoder says about the offending offset.
- [check-schema-fk-delete-path-indexed] ERROR — the schema snapshot at freightworks/services/core-api/migrations/schema.snapshot.sql is not valid UTF-8
